  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that multiprofile with pca_n2000/resnet50/avgpool/concat (config_008, acc 0.619) dramatically outperforms all singleprofile configurations (~0.52–0.53), confirming that multiprofile is the key design lever. However, we have only tested one aggregation strategy (avgpool) in the multiprofile setting. Aggregation determines how multiple profiles are combined before fusion and is arguably the most impactful untested design choice in this regime—transformer aggregation could capture profile-to-profile interactions that a simple average misses. config_006 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, transformer, concat) changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding every other factor identical to config_008, giving a clean single-variable comparison. This is the best use of the next budget slot because it isolates the highest-uncertainty, highest-impact design decision in our currently best-performing family, and the result will directly inform whether further investment in multiprofile transformer-based models is warranted."
}

